# Canonical author identity.
#
# git reads this for `shortlog`, `log`, `blame` and `check-mailmap`, so one
# person committing under several name/email pairs is reported once instead of
# fragmenting the contributor list. It rewrites nothing: the commit objects and
# their signatures are untouched, only how git *displays* them.
#
# Mapping by commit email (the trailing `<...>`) collapses every name spelling
# that used that address, so `JP <joepetjr@gmail.com>` and
# `Joe Petrucelli <joepetjr@gmail.com>` both resolve without a line each.
#
# Bot identities (dependabot[bot], buddy-prod) are deliberately left alone —
# they are not this person and should stay distinct in the log.

Joe Petrucelli <backroadcreativeco@gmail.com> <joepetjr@gmail.com>
Joe Petrucelli <backroadcreativeco@gmail.com> <joepetjr@users.noreply.github.com>
